    <string name="disc_title">Accessibility access</string>
    <string name="disc_body">To block apps, NEELAXMI Focus needs to use Android\'s Accessibility service.\n\nWhat it does:\n• Notices which app comes to the front (its package name) so it can show a block screen for apps you chose.\n• While strict mode is on, it recognises this app\'s own Settings pages (app info, uninstall, accessibility) and covers them, to make switching protection off deliberate.\n\nWhat it never does:\n• It does not read what you type, your messages, passwords or other apps\' content.\n• Nothing is stored or sent anywhere. This build has no internet permission.\n\nYou can turn it off any time in Settings → Accessibility. Strict mode is a strong speed bump, not an unbreakable lock.</string>
