    <string name="limits_title">What cannot be guaranteed</string>
    <string name="limits_text">Android does not let an ordinary app protect itself completely. Force-stopping the app, revoking its permissions, uninstalling it (including from a computer or in safe mode), or switching off the accessibility service from a settings screen this app does not recognise will end blocking. Strict mode makes those steps slower and deliberate; it cannot prevent them.</string>
